       '{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"Clause 28 (Set-Off). This Clause sets out the terms relating to Set-Off in accordance with the LMA recommended form for investment grade syndicated facilities and market practice for wholesale international bank financings documented under English law."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"28.1 Lender set-off rights. The Borrower and each Finance Party acknowledge that the provisions of this sub-clause reflect standard LMA drafting for investment grade borrowers and are subject to facility-specific negotiation recorded in the term sheet and Schedule 1 (Facility Particulars)."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Without limiting the generality of sub-clause 28.1, each Obligor shall procure that all actions required to give full effect to Lender set-off rights are completed within the timeframes and according to the procedures customary for a syndicated term facility of this nature, including delivery of certificates, opinions and evidence reasonably requested by the Agent acting on the instructions of the Majority Lenders."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Agent may, after consultation with the Borrower where practicable, issue guidance or process notes to the Lenders regarding operational matters arising under sub-clause 28.1, provided that such guidance does not amend the legal obligations of the Obligors without a formal amendment to the Finance Documents."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"In negotiating sub-clause 28.1, the Borrower and the Lenders typically consider counsel comments against the LMA recommended form, internal credit policy requirements, and any side letter or term sheet provisions agreed at mandate stage. Any deviation from the LMA baseline is recorded in the execution version of the Finance Documents."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Worked example (illustrative only): where Lender set-off rights applies to the Facility offered to Pacific Rim Holdings Ltd., the Agent will coordinate with the Borrower and the Security Agent to ensure timelines, document versions and evidence standards match those set out in Schedule 2 (Conditions Precedent) and the internal checklist maintained by Meridian Global Banking Corporation."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"28.2 Netting of matured obligations. The Borrower and each Finance Party acknowledge that the provisions of this sub-clause reflect standard LMA drafting for investment grade borrowers and are subject to facility-specific negotiation recorded in the term sheet and Schedule 1 (Facility Particulars)."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Without limiting the generality of sub-clause 28.2, each Obligor shall procure that all actions required to give full effect to Netting of matured obligations are completed within the timeframes and according to the procedures customary for a syndicated term facility of this nature, including delivery of certificates, opinions and evidence reasonably requested by the Agent acting on the instructions of the Majority Lenders."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Agent may, after consultation with the Borrower where practicable, issue guidance or process notes to the Lenders regarding operational matters arising under sub-clause 28.2, provided that such guidance does not amend the legal obligations of the Obligors without a formal amendment to the Finance Documents."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"In negotiating sub-clause 28.2, the Borrower and the Lenders typically consider counsel comments against the LMA recommended form, internal credit policy requirements, and any side letter or term sheet provisions agreed at mandate stage. Any deviation from the LMA baseline is recorded in the execution version of the Finance Documents."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Worked example (illustrative only): where Netting of matured obligations applies to the Facility offered to Pacific Rim Holdings Ltd., the Agent will coordinate with the Borrower and the Security Agent to ensure timelines, document versions and evidence standards match those set out in Schedule 2 (Conditions Precedent) and the internal checklist maintained by Meridian Global Banking Corporation."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"28.3 Notification of set-off. The Borrower and each Finance Party acknowledge that the provisions of this sub-clause reflect standard LMA drafting for investment grade borrowers and are subject to facility-specific negotiation recorded in the term sheet and Schedule 1 (Facility Particulars)."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Without limiting the generality of sub-clause 28.3, each Obligor shall procure that all actions required to give full effect to Notification of set-off are completed within the timeframes and according to the procedures customary for a syndicated term facility of this nature, including delivery of certificates, opinions and evidence reasonably requested by the Agent acting on the instructions of the Majority Lenders."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Agent may, after consultation with the Borrower where practicable, issue guidance or process notes to the Lenders regarding operational matters arising under sub-clause 28.3, provided that such guidance does not amend the legal obligations of the Obligors without a formal amendment to the Finance Documents."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"In negotiating sub-clause 28.3, the Borrower and the Lenders typically consider counsel comments against the LMA recommended form, internal credit policy requirements, and any side letter or term sheet provisions agreed at mandate stage. Any deviation from the LMA baseline is recorded in the execution version of the Finance Documents."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Worked example (illustrative only): where Notification of set-off applies to the Facility offered to Pacific Rim Holdings Ltd., the Agent will coordinate with the Borrower and the Security Agent to ensure timelines, document versions and evidence standards match those set out in Schedule 2 (Conditions Precedent) and the internal checklist maintained by Meridian Global Banking Corporation."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"28.4 Continuing obligations after set-off. The Borrower and each Finance Party acknowledge that the provisions of this sub-clause reflect standard LMA drafting for investment grade borrowers and are subject to facility-specific negotiation recorded in the term sheet and Schedule 1 (Facility Particulars)."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Without limiting the generality of sub-clause 28.4, each Obligor shall procure that all actions required to give full effect to Continuing obligations after set-off are completed within the timeframes and according to the procedures customary for a syndicated term facility of this nature, including delivery of certificates, opinions and evidence reasonably requested by the Agent acting on the instructions of the Majority Lenders."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Agent may, after consultation with the Borrower where practicable, issue guidance or process notes to the Lenders regarding operational matters arising under sub-clause 28.4, provided that such guidance does not amend the legal obligations of the Obligors without a formal amendment to the Finance Documents."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"In negotiating sub-clause 28.4, the Borrower and the Lenders typically consider counsel comments against the LMA recommended form, internal credit policy requirements, and any side letter or term sheet provisions agreed at mandate stage. Any deviation from the LMA baseline is recorded in the execution version of the Finance Documents."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Worked example (illustrative only): where Continuing obligations after set-off applies to the Facility offered to Pacific Rim Holdings Ltd., the Agent will coordinate with the Borrower and the Security Agent to ensure timelines, document versions and evidence standards match those set out in Schedule 2 (Conditions Precedent) and the internal checklist maintained by Meridian Global Banking Corporation."},{"type":"paragraph",